      "writtenOn": "2019-10-24T17:42:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what exactly goes wrong when you just implement this as %f? We already have -mfloat-abi\u003dhard compiled in all boards, indicating an assumption that floating point support is available. I also see a few cases where floating point is used, though that code may not be activated on all boards.\n\nIt seems to me like it should be fine to implement the standard %f, even with the automatic promotion to double. You\u0027re already hiding this support behind CONFIG_FPU. If we come across boards that somehow support 32-bit floats but not 64-bit doubles, then -mfloat-abi\u003dhard -mfpu\u003dfpv4-sp-d16 was the wrong set of compiler options anyway. So those boards should be compiled with something different, like -mfloat-abi\u003dsoftfp. But I don\u0027t actually think any such hardware exists.",
